{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.CyclicQuantumDilog","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.CyclicQuantumDilog","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Intervals","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicQDilog_class_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicQDilog_class_shift","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CyclicQuantumDilog.lean#L131-L146","doc":"**The class-difference law** (the χ-shadow of (21)): for any\nmonoid hom `χ : R →* M` into a commutative monoid killing m-th powers,\n`χ(1 − x^m)^r · χ(D_ζ(ζ^r x)) = χ(D_ζ(x))` — the root-difference law\n`Δclass = −r·class(1−X)` verified numerically by every ε_m probe. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicQDilog_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicQDilog_shift","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CyclicQuantumDilog.lean#L61-L129","doc":"**The CGZ shift identity (21)**, generically: with `ζ^m = 1`, the\ncyclotomic factorization, and `r ≤ m`,\n`(1 − x^m)^r · D_ζ(ζ^r x) = (∏_{k<r}(1 − ζ^k x)^m) · D_ζ(x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicQDilog","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicQDilog","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CyclicQuantumDilog.lean#L56-L59","doc":"The cyclic quantum dilogarithm `D_ζ(x) = ∏_{k<m} (1 − ζ^k x)^k`\n(CGZ eqn (8)); the `k = 0` factor is `1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}